    "title": "How many students were enrolled in Bowie County schools during 2023-24 school year?",
    "text": "Texas State Board Of Education Chair Keven Ellis (2024) | twitter.com/KevenEllisDC\nTexas State Board Of Education Chair Keven Ellis (2024) | twitter.com/KevenEllisDC\nTexas Education Agency.\nAt the time, Bowie County had the 55th largest enrollment in the state.\nData also showed that white students made up 48.8% of the student body, the largest percentage in Bowie County schools, followed by Black students at 30%, Hispanic students at 12.5%, Asian students at 1%, American Indian students at 0.4%, Pacific Islander students at 0.1% and multiracial students at 7.1%.\nUnderfunding is a frequently cited challenge facing the state's school district. According to a 2024 report from the Texas Education Agency, per-pupil funding has not increased since 2019, despite inflation rates rising by more than 20% since then.\n“As a result, many districts in our very own Central Texas region are being forced to cut back on essential programs, services, consider school closures, and adopt deficit budgets just to provide students with the education that they deserve,” Hutto ISD Trustee James Matlock stated in an interview.\nSchool name | Total enrollment in 2022-23 | Total enrollment in 2023-24 | % change |\n---|---|---|---|\nCrestview Elementary School | 584 | 547 | -6.3% |\nDekalb Elementary School | 321 | 366 | 14% |\nDekalb High School | 272 | 278 | 2.2% |\nDekalb Middle School | 235 | 257 | 9.4% |\nEschool Prep | 227 | 411 | 81.1% |\nHighland Park Elementary School | 364 | 403 | 10.7% |\nHooks Elementary School | 317 | 318 | 0.3% |\nHooks High School | 319 | 309 | -3.1% |\nHooks Junior High School | 284 | 263 | -7.4% |\nHubbard ISD | 77 | 67 | -13% |\nJames Bowie Elementary School | 212 | 221 | 4.2% |\nJames Bowie High School | 140 | 154 | 10% |\nJames Bowie Middle School | 132 | 130 | -1.5% |\nLeary Elementary School | 93 | 120 | 29% |\nLiberty-Eylau Early Childhood Center | 323 | 296 | -8.4% |\nLiberty-Eylau Elementary School | 575 | 571 | -0.7% |\nLiberty-Eylau High School | 532 | 536 | 0.8% |\nLiberty-Eylau Middle School | 573 | 582 | 1.6% |\nMalta Elementary School | 220 | 212 | -3.6% |\nMargaret Fischer Davis Elementary School | 530 | 509 | -4% |\nMartha & Josh Morriss Math & Engineering Elementary School | 358 | 360 | 0.6% |\nMaud School | 476 | 456 | -4.2% |\nNash Elementary School | 677 | 656 | -3.1% |\nNew Boston High School | 321 | 343 | 6.9% |\nNew Boston Middle School | 249 | 252 | 1.2% |\nOptions | 69 | 69 | 0% |\nPaul Laurence Dunbar Early Education Center | 296 | 304 | 2.7% |\nPleasant Grove High School | 796 | 753 | -5.4% |\nPleasant Grove Intermediate School | 483 | 483 | 0% |\nPleasant Grove Middle School | 501 | 529 | 5.6% |\nPremier High School of Texarkana | 142 | 129 | -9.2% |\nRed Lick Elementary School | 306 | 297 | -2.9% |\nRed Lick Middle School | 221 | 222 | 0.5% |\nRedwater Elementary School | 313 | 338 | 8% |\nRedwater High School | 339 | 351 | 3.5% |\nRedwater Junior High School | 180 | 169 | -6.1% |\nRedwater Middle School | 227 | 251 | 10.6% |\nSpring Lake Park Elementary School | 408 | 374 | -8.3% |\nTexas High School | 1,719 | 1,762 | 2.5% |\nTexas Middle School | 1,413 | 1,361 | -3.7% |\nTheron Jones Early Literacy Center | 386 | 339 | -12.2% |\nWaggoner Creek Elementary School | 338 | 347 | 2.7% |\nWake Village Elementary School | 579 | 548 | -5.4% |\nWestlawn Elementary School | 346 | 342 | -1.2% |",
